{
  "_": "ONE table, read by both readers of a card's agent (docs/hub/cards.md, \"How a card's agent is worked out\"): Scripts/Get-PromptFileStatus.ps1 Resolve-P20CardAgent, Get-P20CommitCoAuthors, Get-P20ModelByCoAuthor and ConvertFrom-P20GitMessages (tkTestToolkit -Triage), and agent/core/parsers.py resolve_card_agent, commit_co_authors and git_messages, with agent/core/models.py model_by_co_author (Tests/test_parsers.py). models is the map every row is read against -- its own, so the table does not move when Config/models.json grows -- and current its current block (a worker size -> the model id it means today); a row with current null is read against a map with no current block. rows: each row's lines are joined with LF, or CRLF when crlf is true, into a card's text; label is the card's issue's worker label ('' for none); messages is short hash -> commit message, or null for not read; order is the sources' order, and a row with none runs under the shipped one, consts.json models.agentSources (line, assigned, trailer, none: it never reads the label, which a caller asks for by passing an order that names it). expected is {id, family, source}. coAuthors: a commit message -> the names its Co-Authored-By trailers carry, in order. byCoAuthor: a trailer name -> the model id whose coAuthor it is, trimmed and ignoring case, or null. gitLog: git log's --format=%x00%H%x1f%B output -> short hash (seven characters, lower case) -> message, trailing line endings removed. If the two halves ever disagree about a row, one of them is wrong.",
